16. GroupBy — Very Important ⭐

groupby() is one of the most important Pandas concepts for Data Analysis.

| Method        | Use                                     | Example                                                 |
| ------------- | --------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |
| `groupby()`   | Group data                              | `df.groupby("City")`                                    |
| `sum()`       | Sum groups                              | `df.groupby("City")["Sales"].sum()`                     |
| `mean()`      | Average groups                          | `df.groupby("City")["Sales"].mean()`                    |
| `count()`     | Count groups                            | `df.groupby("City")["Sales"].count()`                   |
| `min()`       | Minimum per group                       | `df.groupby("City")["Sales"].min()`                     |
| `max()`       | Maximum per group                       | `df.groupby("City")["Sales"].max()`                     |
| `agg()`       | Multiple aggregations                   | `df.groupby("City")["Sales"].agg(["sum","mean","max"])` |
| `transform()` | Group calculation while preserving rows | `df.groupby("City")["Sales"].transform("mean")`         |


Example
df.groupby("City")["Sales"].sum()

Means:

Group the data by City and calculate total Sales for each city.
